  "question": {
    "text": "The number of distinct complex number(s) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>, such that <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> is purely imaginary, is/are equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#952;</mi></math><br />Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> is purely imaginary<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Possible value of <math><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mn>150</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mn>90</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mn>270</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mn>210</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mn>330</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  }
